The brief calls for a titled list of eight status-tagged items with a status filter. I used a heading as the root, a segmented control for the filter, and an entity list for the items. The catalog has no generic container that references child components by id, so the components are flat, in top-down order.

<a2ui-json>
[
  {
    "version": "v0.9.1",
    "createSurface": {
      "surfaceId": "status-items",
      "catalogId": "https://a2uicatalog.ai/catalog/c-data-display.json"
    }
  },
  {
    "version": "v0.9.1",
    "updateComponents": {
      "surfaceId": "status-items",
      "components": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "component": "heading",
          "text": "Work Items"
        },
        {
          "id": "status-filter",
          "component": "segmented_control",
          "name": "status_filter",
          "selected_value": "all",
          "options": "[{\"label\": \"All\", \"value\": \"all\"}, {\"label\": \"Open\", \"value\": \"open\"}, {\"label\": \"In progress\", \"value\": \"in_progress\"}, {\"label\": \"Blocked\", \"value\": \"blocked\"}, {\"label\": \"Done\", \"value\": \"done\"}]",
          "accessibility": {
            "label": "Filter by status"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "item-list",
          "component": "entity_list",
          "items": {
            "type": "array",
            "description": "List of {name, subtitle, status, meta} entries.",
            "value": [
              {
                "name": "Set up CI pipeline",
                "subtitle": "Configure build runners for the main branch",
                "status": "Done",
                "meta": "Owner: Priya"
              },
              {
                "name": "Migrate auth tokens",
                "subtitle": "Move session storage to the new key format",
                "status": "In progress",
                "meta": "Owner: Marcus"
              },
              {
                "name": "Draft API rate-limit policy",
                "subtitle": "Define per-tenant request quotas",
                "status": "Open",
                "meta": "Owner: Lena"
              },
              {
                "name": "Update billing webhooks",
                "subtitle": "Add retry handling for failed events",
                "status": "Blocked",
                "meta": "Owner: Dev"
              },
              {
                "name": "Audit access logs",
                "subtitle": "Verify log retention settings",
                "status": "In progress",
                "meta": "Owner: Sam"
              },
              {
                "name": "Write onboarding guide",
                "subtitle": "Cover first-run setup steps",
                "status": "Done",
                "meta": "Owner: Ana"
              },
              {
                "name": "Load test checkout flow",
                "subtitle": "Target 500 concurrent users",
                "status": "Open",
                "meta": "Owner: Jonah"
              },
              {
                "name": "Rotate database credentials",
                "subtitle": "Schedule the rotation window",
                "status": "Blocked",
                "meta": "Owner: Priya"
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  }
]
</a2ui-json>

The filter control is wired to the `status_filter` name, and each item carries its status for filtering. The catalog has no built-in filtering behaviour, so the client must apply the selected value to the item list.
